                "content": "# Fullerton Creek below Fullerton Dam, near Brea, Calif.\n\nLocation. Lat 33\u00b053'40\" long. 117\u00b053'05\" in San Juan Cajon de Santa Ana Grant, on left bank of outlet channel of Fullerton Dam, 1.6 miles southeast of Brea, Orange County\n\nDrainage area.--3.05 sq mi.\n\nRecords available. --October 1941 to September 1952.\n\nGage. Water-stage recorder. Altitude of gage is 260 ft (from topographic map) Average discharge --11 years, 0.21 cfs; median of yearly mean discharges, 0.03 cfs.\n\nExtremes -Maximum discharge during year, 115 cfs Jan. 19 (gage height, 4.06 ft); no flow during many months. 1941-52: Maximum discharge, 298 cf's Mar. 16, 1943 (gage height, 3.80 ft); no flow\n\nmost of each year.\n\n8, 1950 (gage height, 3.22 ft), superseding figures published in Water-Supply Paper 1181. Revision.--The maximum discharge for water year 1950 has been revised to 66 cfs Feb.\n\nRemarks.--Records good. Flow regulated by Fullerton flood-control reservoir (capacity, 743 acre-ft).\n\nRating table, water year 1951-52 (gage height, in feet, and discharge, in cubic feet per second)\n\n<table><tr><th>0.85</th><th>O</th><th>1,5</th><th>4.1</th></tr><tr><td>.9</td><td>.1</td><td>1.6</td><td>5.9</td></tr><tr><td>1.0</td><td>.2</td><td>1,8</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1.1</td><td>.3</td><td>2,0</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>1.2</td><td>.7</td><td>2.5</td><td>32</td></tr><tr><td>1.3</td><td>1.4</td><td>3.0</td><td>55</td></tr><tr><td>1.4</td><td>2,6</td><td>3.5</td><td>81</td></tr></table>\n\nDischarge, in cubic feet per second, water year October 1951 to September 1952",
